{"content":"Confirmed: `internal/scheduler` is only imported by its own test files (`example_test.go`, `integration_test.go`), never by server startup code. And `server/runner/memopayload` is only used for its `RebuildMemoPayload` helper function inline in request handlers (`memo_service.go:108,447`), not as a background runner — its `Runner`/`RunOnce` type is never instantiated anywhere.\n\nq28.\n\n**Background workers actually started by the server** (`server/server.go:153` `startBackgroundRunners`, called from `Start()` at server.go:129):\n\n- **S3 presign runner** — `server/runner/s3presign.Runner` (`server/runner/s3presign/runner.go`). Trigger: an internal `time.Ticker` firing every 12 hours (`runnerInterval = time.Hour * 12`, runner.go:27,30), started via `s3presignRunner.Run(s3Context)` in a goroutine (`server/server.go:167-170`), plus one synchronous `RunOnce` call immediately at startup (`server/server.go:163`).\n- **In-memory store cache cleanup loop** — `store/cache.Cache.cleanupLoop` (`store/cache/cache.go:200`). Trigger: a `time.Ticker` on `c.config.CleanupInterval` (default 5 minutes, set in `store/store.go:42`). Started as a goroutine inside `cache.New()` (`store/cache/cache.go:76,83`), which fires whenever `store.New()` constructs the store's three caches (`store/store.go:51-53`) — so effectively at server boot.\n- **Async webhook dispatch pool** — `internal/webhook/webhook.go:42-51`. Trigger: not time-based — 4 goroutines started in `init()` consume from a bounded channel (`asyncPostQueue`, cap 128) whenever `webhook.PostAsync` enqueues a payload (called from `server/router/api/v1/memo_service_webhooks.go:43,71`).\n- **Async email dispatch pool** — `internal/email/email.go:16-36`. Same pattern: 2 goroutines started in `init()`, triggered by items pushed onto `asyncEmailQueue` via `email.SendAsync`.\n\n**Unused scheduling infrastructure:** the `internal/scheduler` package (`internal/scheduler/scheduler.go`, `parser.go`, `middleware.go`) implements a full cron-style job scheduler — `Scheduler.Register`/`Start`/`Stop`, cron expression parsing (`ParseCronExpression`), timeout/recovery/logging middleware. It is exercised only by its own `example_test.go` and `integration_test.go`; no production code (`server/server.go`, `cmd/memos/main.go`, or anywhere else) imports `internal/scheduler`. It is dead/unused infrastructure as far as the running server is concerned.\n\nAlso notable: `server/runner/memopayload.Runner` (with its ticker-free `RunOnce` batch job) is defined but never instantiated by the server — only the package-level helper `RebuildMemoPayload` is called, and that's invoked synchronously inline from memo create/update request handlers (`server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go:108,447`), not as a background runner.","iteration":19,"turn":1,"type":"assistant"}
